    "operationId": "error_tracking_bypass_rules_create",
    "title": "Create error tracking bypass rule",
    "category": "Error tracking",
    "description": "Create a rate limit bypass rule for the current project. Exception events matching the rule skip both the project-wide and per-issue exception rate limits and are always ingested. Provide `filters` with at least one condition — empty match-all rules are rejected; to stop rate limiting entirely, update the rate limits via error-tracking-settings-update instead. Keep filters scoped to the specific errors that must never be dropped: bypassed events are ingested and billed even during error spikes, so a broad rule can cause unbounded volume.",
    "requiredScopes": ["error_tracking:write"],
